@startuml
title Shadow - Login through Authentik (ADR-017)

actor Browser
participant "Application ingress\nCaddy / same-origin API" as Caddy
participant "FastAPI" as API
participant "Identity ingress\nCaddy id host" as IdCaddy
participant "Authentik\nOIDC provider 'Shadow'" as Provider
database PostgreSQL as DB

note over Provider
  Own Authentik instance, pinned version, own logical database.
  Confidential web client; authorization code with S256 PKCE (a policy requires it).
  Enrollment by invitation; email verified; passkey or TOTP always required.
  email_verified is true only while the address equals the verified address.
end note

note over Browser, Caddy
  Development: https://app.localhost and https://id.app.localhost (local Caddy).
  Production: https://shadow.lupaus.eu and https://id.shadow.lupaus.eu (step 086A).
  The backend reaches Authentik inside the Docker network (OIDC_INTERNAL_BASE_URL),
  sending the public Host and scheme; Authentik trusts them only from the backend.
end note

Browser -> Caddy : GET /api/v1/auth/login?return_to=/workspace
Caddy -> API : Fixed Host/proto and trusted client IP
API -> DB : Store hashed state + browser binding, nonce, PKCE
API --> Browser : 302 Authentik authorization URL\nHttpOnly pre-auth cookie
Browser -> IdCaddy : Authorization request
IdCaddy -> Provider : Proxied
Provider --> Browser : Sign-in flow: passkey, or password + second factor
Provider --> Browser : Redirect with code + state to the exact callback
Browser -> Caddy : GET /api/v1/auth/callback?code=...&state=...
note right of Caddy
  Access log replaces code, state,
  error and error_description with REDACTED.
end note
Caddy -> API : Callback with fixed proxy headers
API -> DB : Atomically consume browser-bound transaction
API -> Provider : Redeem code with confidential client + verifier\n(internal address, public Host)
Provider --> API : Token response
API -> API : Validate signature, exact issuer, audience, nonce and claims;\nrequire email_verified
note right of DB
  Login never creates Users (accounts for new people come with tenants).
  A verified email links the identity to a pre-provisioned User once;
  an unknown or unverified person gets the generic failure and no session.
end note
API -> DB : Guarded first-link, or exact (issuer, subject)\nCreate hashed opaque application session\nKeep the ID token only for sign-out
API --> Browser : 303 clean local path\nSecure HttpOnly SameSite=Strict cookie
Browser -> Caddy : GET SPA and /api with session cookie
Caddy -> API : Same-origin /api request
API -> DB : Reload active User and session
API --> Browser : Application data only; no provider token

== Sign-out ==
Browser -> API : POST /api/v1/auth/logout (Origin + CSRF)
API -> DB : Delete the session
API --> Browser : logoutUrl with id_token_hint and the exact return address
Browser -> IdCaddy : end-session
IdCaddy -> Provider : Invalidation flow ends the Authentik session
Provider --> Browser : Redirect to https://app.localhost/login

@enduml
